## Problem

### Farmer asks:

> “Will this buyer pay?”
> 

### Buyer asks:

> “Will this farmer deliver what I ordered?”
> 

---

## Solution

**Digital transaction proof = every sale is recorded in the app, so payment and delivery disputes are traceable.**

Example:

**Farmer sells 1T → Buyer accepts → ₹30,000 payment → Digital record/proof**

**So: Sale + delivery + payment history = proof → reduces money/payment disputes.**

### Research question

Ask buyers:

> “Before buying from a new supplier, what proof do you require?”
> 

You'll likely discover the actual trust requirements:

- past transaction history
- sample
- quality certificate
- FPO identity
- GST/business documents
- payment terms
- quantity guarantee
- delivery history

Those are the things your platform should encode. and make ensure trust issue is resolved with like status when will be paid the amount if not now then extendend date ,fine,etc 

